  "text": "Solution 3 is the most likely correct answer, though I could not verify it against the literature.\n\n- **Solution 2 (k = 3)** is contradicted by the Braun–Oréfice-Okamoto paper, which is titled around degree-4 submersions and, as I recall, proves injectivity for $\\deg p \\le 4$. Its cubic-case argument cannot be the frontier.\n- **Solution 1 (k = 5)** claims injectivity for $\\deg p \\le 5$ and a counterexample with $\\deg p = 6$. The degree-5 injectivity claim is the part I doubt: it is not the established result I recall, and it conflicts with Solution 3's degree-5 counterexample.\n- **Solution 3 (k = 4)** is consistent with the degree-4 injectivity result. Its key extra claim is a non-injective example with $\\deg p = 5$, attributed to Braun and Fernandes. I cannot confirm that example from memory, so this is the weak point.\n\nSolutions 1 and 3 cannot both be right, and Solution 3 is the only one consistent with the degree-4 result I am fairly confident of, so I favour it.\n\nCHOICE: 3",
